sw/doc/ - cgra documentation
============================

Three hand-written sources, no generators beyond makeinfo/groff:

    cgra.1        man(1) - the command-line tool reference
    cgra.5        man(5) - the .cgra configuration file format
    cgra.texi     GNU info manual (root file; @includes the chapters below)

The texinfo manual is modular - one @include per chapter:

    overview.texi       what cgra is, the stack, design intent
    invocation.texi     command line, device resolution, input/output
    commands.texi       the full command reference (@deffn per command)
    configuration.texi  the .cgra language, tutorial style
    stdlib.texi         the bundled standard library
    dataflow.texi       how patterns map onto the array
    protocol.texi       the UART wire protocol, in brief
    environment.texi    environment variables
    examples.texi       worked examples
    files.texi          where config and state live

Build / read (make -f ../sw.mk <target>)
----------------------------------------
    info     ../build/cgra.info      (makeinfo)
    man      lint + render cgra.1 and cgra.5 -> ../build/*.txt
    doc      both of the above

    man ./cgra.1        # or:  man ./cgra.5
    info ../build/cgra.info

Install
-------
    install -Dm644 cgra.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/cgra.1
    install -Dm644 cgra.5 /usr/local/share/man/man5/cgra.5
    install -Dm644 ../build/cgra.info /usr/local/share/info/cgra.info

Library API is documented separately: libcgra(3) in lib/doc/.
